  speak for myself as a black woman so I  take great offense between you know when  when the media wants to reduce black  people to voices in a collective box  that have to be relegated to  spokespeople Peter you don't have a  white spokesperson that speaks on your  behalf to you maybe maybe you do and I  don't know about it but I think I missed  that memo so when you look at Cornel  West he's making a lot of money writing  books about what black people should  think and do and now he's the voice of  black people he teaches this stuff at  Princeton Allen West on the other hand  is telling people speak for yourself he  was a loud mouth in a good way  congressman he tells it like it is  and he is much more of a hero and a  champion in me for the cause of black  American than Cornel West will ever be  so they're a little bit from crystal  right her new book con job how Democrats  gave us crime sanctuary cities abortion  profiteering and racial division  you're watching book TV on c-span too  every day books are reviewed by  publications throughout the country  here's a look at some recently reviewed  books chief foreign correspondent for  NBC News Richard angles new book on the  Middle East was reviewed by Kevin  Canfield for the Kansas City Star he  writes that at heart the book is a  nerve-wracking autobiography by a  journalist on the front lines covering  Wars and terrorism in Lebanon Israel  Gaza Iraq and Syria on another level  it's an informative portrait of a  troubled region one that has been unduly  influenced by charlatans and madmen and  poorly served by two consecutive  American presidents in this Sunday's New  York Times Book Review david ershon skee  a history professor at new york  university reviewed adam Cohen's new  book about state-sponsored sterilization  in the United States and the  precedent-setting Supreme Court case  buck V Bell professor of schinsky notes  that at its height from the late 1920s  through the 1950s forced sterilization  in the 